            <ArticleTitle>Rheumatoid hand. Practical approach to assessment and management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1303-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rheumatoid arthritis is a systemic inflammatory disease with a predilection for the synovial tissues. Its diverse involvement can be demonstrated in the hand, where several anatomical structures can be affected simultaneously. Proper management requires attention to this principle, and a complete diagnostic evaluation will help to identify correctly the cause of the patient's functional limitation and pain. We present a practical approach to managing rheumatoid arthritis in the hand.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
